# Zyphera TCG — Environment Variables
PORT=3000
MONGODB_URI=mongodb://localhost:27017/zypheratcg
SESSION_SECRET=zyphera-tcg-session-secret-change-me-in-production
NODE_ENV=development

# The site's public origin, no trailing slash. Used to build canonical URLs,
# the sitemap, feed product links, and — critically — the Google OAuth
# redirect URI on /admin/distribution. Google rejects a relative redirect
# URI, so leaving this unset makes connecting Merchant Center fail with an
# error from Google rather than from us.
SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Optional. When set, /feed/google.xml requires ?key=<value>. Everything in
# the feed is already public on the product pages, so this is not protecting
# a secret — it just stops the file being trivially discoverable and scraped
# on a loop. Leave unset for an open feed, which is the normal arrangement.
FEED_TOKEN=

# Partner Experience Settings
ENCRYPTION_KEY=12345678901234567890123456789012
PARTNER_EXPERIENCE_API_KEY=
PARTNER_EXPERIENCE_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=2500
PARTNER_EXPERIENCE_MAX_RETRIES=1

# Required for the post-purchase pipeline (/thank-you) to trust an incoming
# order-import redirect. Must be set to the EXACT SAME value as
# THANK_YOU_SIGNING_SECRET on the NorthbridgeAI deployment — it signs the
# completed-purchase data, this server verifies it before creating an order.
# Without this set (or on a mismatch), no order is ever created from an
# imported redirect. Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
THANK_YOU_SIGNING_SECRET=

# ── Transactional email (ZeptoMail) ───────────────────────
# THE VARIABLES THAT WERE MISSING. Every order confirmation this shop
# ever "sent" was written to stdout and dropped, because these were
# never documented here and so were never set on the server. If nothing
# below is set, /admin/emails says "Not sending" and every message is
# logged with status `skipped` — which is at least visible, but nobody
# gets an email.
#
# WHY NOT ZOHO MAIL: Zoho removed SMTP/IMAP/POP from the free plan, so
# there is no credential that would authenticate. Zoho Mail also is not
# meant for application email even on a paid plan — Zoho's own answer is
# ZeptoMail, which is billed per message with no monthly floor.
#
# Zoho Mail keeps the human mailboxes (support@, returns@, privacy@).
# Nothing here touches them. Replies to these emails go to support@ via
# MAIL_REPLY_TO below, so a customer who hits Reply reaches a person.
#
# Get these from ZeptoMail → Mail Agents → your agent → SMTP:
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASS=
#
# Defaults are ZeptoMail's own endpoint and do not need setting. Change
# them only if you move providers — everything speaks ordinary SMTP.
#SMTP_HOST=smtp.zeptomail.com
#SMTP_PORT=587
#
# The From address. Send-only: it does not need to be a real mailbox,
# but the DOMAIN must be verified in ZeptoMail with SPF and DKIM, or
# Gmail will refuse it. See docs/email-setup.md.
#MAIL_FROM=orders@zypheratcg.com
#MAIL_FROM_NAME=Zyphera TCG
#
# Where replies land. MUST be a real, monitored mailbox — a bouncing
# Reply-To is a genuine deliverability penalty, and a customer replying
# into a void is a support ticket that did not need to happen. Defaults
# to the support address in config/company.js.
#MAIL_REPLY_TO=support@zypheratcg.com

# ── Order push notifications ──────────────────────────────
# Everything except the key lives in config/push.js and needs no
# environment variable: sound, critical alerts and volume are set there
# because they never change. Each still accepts an override below if a
# particular deploy needs a different value.
#
# Bark (iPhone) — https://github.com/Finb/Bark
# The ONLY required value. Install "Bark - Custom Notifications" from the
# App Store; the key is the last path segment of the URL it shows you.
# Deliberately kept out of the repo: anyone holding it can push
# notifications to the phone, which is a route for a convincing fake such
# as "Payment failed, tap to fix". Unset means no notifications, not an
# error. Rotate it in the Bark app and update this value if it ever leaks.
BARK_KEY=
#
# Overrides for the config/push.js defaults (cha-ching / critical / 7).
# See docs/push-sound.md for importing the sound and for the iOS Critical
# Alerts permission, which is required in addition to BARK_CRITICAL.
#BARK_SOUND=cha-ching
# active (default) | critical
# active is an ordinary notification: sound plays normally with the
# ringer on, and there is no banner. It is silent on a silenced phone and
# is suppressed by Focus modes.
# critical rings through the silent switch and Focus, but iOS stamps
# every critical alert with a red "CRITICAL" banner that cannot be turned
# off, and it needs the Critical Alerts permission granted to Bark on the
# phone. See docs/push-sound.md.
#BARK_LEVEL=active
#BARK_VOLUME=7
#BARK_SERVER=https://api.day.app
#BARK_ICON=

# ntfy (Android, or a second device) — https://ntfy.sh
# Off unless a topic is set. Anyone who knows a public topic name can read
# everything published to it, so treat the name as a password.
#NTFY_TOPIC=
#NTFY_SERVER=https://ntfy.sh
#NTFY_TOKEN=

# ── Google Ads ──────────────────────────────────────────
# The tag id is public (it ships in page source) and defaults to the live
# account, so the site-wide tag works with no configuration. Set this only
# to point the store at a different Ads account.
#GOOGLE_ADS_ID=AW-18382200056
#
# The conversion label from Goals -> Conversions -> your Purchase action.
# Committed alongside the id, since the conversion is gated on the pair and a
# label set without an id (or the reverse) reports nothing at all. Set this
# only to report into a different account's purchase action.
#GOOGLE_ADS_PURCHASE_LABEL=IOe_CKPw5eocEPi5qL1E
